**How to implement.** The quick swap as a semantic message: another item into one slot is another setup, an existing one or a new one (001 §J 'Quick swap: … choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one'; 001 §P `SwapSlot`; the S8.2 brief). The slot bar that sends it is S8.4's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `SwapSlot of Library.ElementId * ItemId`, with a one-line doc: the table as the setup that holds this item in that slot. (2) Its arm resolves the slot, the item and its choice and refuses as `AssignSlot` does (step 263), with `Not swapped — <e.describe>`. The swapped slots are the table's with that slot `withItem item choice` (step 258), each `recordedWith model.kitItems`; the fresh name is `active.name.nextFreeAmong` the kit's setup names for `activeSetupOpt = Some active` and `SetupName.firstFree` of them otherwise (step 255). `Setup.swapTarget swapped model.kitSetups fresh` (step 258): `SwitchToHeldSetup s` is `ActivateSetup s.name`'s update (step 260) and writes nothing, so a read-only kit takes it; `CreateSwappedSetup s` is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, and otherwise recorded through `recordSetup` (step 260): on `Ok`, `kitSetups` holds it in name order, `activeSetupOpt` is `Some s`, `elements` are the swapped slots and `kitStatus` is `Created setup '<name>' by the swap.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. The setup swapped from is never written. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 260, 263), whose kit holds `QZ` (the glass plate at version 1) and `QZ2` (the 2 mm plate at version 1) and a table of a source, a sample and the seeded detector: `SwapSlot switches to the kit's setup that holds the swapped content and writes nothing`: with `Bench A` created holding `QZ` and `Bench B` holding `QZ2` (each through `AssignSlot` then `CreateSetup`), and `Bench A` made active again (`ActivateSetup`), `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` makes `Bench B` active and the table its slots, and no kit file's bytes change. `SwapSlot to content no setup holds creates and activates a setup of the next free name, leaving the swapped-from setup as it was`: with only `Bench A` held and active, `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` writes `Bench A (2).setup-json` holding `QZ2` at revision 1, makes it active, and `Bench A`'s file is unchanged; from a table that is no setup yet, the swap creates `Setup 1`. `a kit opened read-only switches setups by a swap but creates none`: over the folder reopened read-only, the swap to `Bench B` switches, and the swap to new content sets `kitStatus` to `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.` and leaves the table, `kitSetups` and every file as they were.

**Acceptance.** After SwapSlot lands, `SwapSlot` MUST switch to the kit's setup holding the swapped content without writing, and otherwise create, record and activate a setup of the next free name, never writing the setup swapped from and creating nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SwapSlot switches to the kit's setup that holds the swapped content and writes nothing`, `SwapSlot to content no setup holds creates and activates a setup of the next free name, leaving the swapped-from setup as it was` and `a kit opened read-only switches setups by a swap but creates none`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
